{
  "name": "Build a B2B lead list with emails from job title, country and company size filters (Apollo alternative) into Google Sheets with Apify",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 760,
        "content": "## Build a B2B lead list with emails from ICP filters\n\n### Who's it for\nFounders and SDRs who want a prospect list by job title, seniority, country, industry and company size, with an email on every row, without an Apollo or Sales Navigator subscription.\n\n### How it works\n1. A Set node holds your filters (edit the values).\n2. **B2B Leads Finder** (`b2bsearch/b2b-leads-finder`) on Apify searches a database of 800M+ professional profiles and returns one row per person who has an email on record: name, title, company, location, LinkedIn URL, email and its type. People without an email are skipped and not charged.\n3. The rows are appended to your Google Sheet, ready for a sequence tool.\n\n### Setup steps\n- Add your Apify credential to the Apify node.\n- Edit `jobTitles`, `countries`, `industries`, `companySizeMin`, `companySizeMax`, `emailType` and `maxResults` in **ICP filters**.\n- Pick the output sheet. Run again with a different sheet to grow the list; use `excludeDatasets` in the Actor to skip people from earlier runs.\n\n### Requirements\n- Apify account. $1.50–$3 per 1,000 leads depending on your Apify plan; 500 leads cost at most $1.50.\n- Google Sheets credential.\n\n### Disclosure\nThe Apify Actor in this template is built by the author of the template. It is pay per result: a miss is a free row."
      },
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -900,
        -220
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "width": 420,
        "height": 300,
        "content": "## 1. Your ICP\nTitle words, two-letter country codes, industry names, employee range. `emailType` = work, personal or any.",
        "color": 7
      },
      "name": "Note: filters",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -380,
        -220
      ]
    },
    {
